From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] media: keep GE playback diagnostics quiet and privacy-safe

GE 11-6's live diagnostics scan pixels and force staging-texture readbacks
even with WINEDEBUG=-all. Remove those diagnostic-only operations and the
client-texture probe that prints the complete source URL. Keep the actual
cross-device, system-memory, and same-device transfer paths unchanged.

Use the existing trace level for GE's routine state/query chatter rather
than warning on normal playback. No channel is added; broad mfplat tracing
remains unsupported for sessions. Also omit the URL from the unknown-MIME
message, which RTSP's unlisted MIME can reach. True failure warnings remain.

This does not change queues, clocks, retry policy, or playback algorithms.
